# `actuarial::life_contingencies::dx_lx`

Deaths between consecutive ages of a life table.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series actuarial::life_contingencies::dx_lx(const pluss::Series &lx);
```

## What It Does

Returns {math}`d_k=l_k-l_{k+1}`: the expected number of deaths in each year, one fewer value than `lx`. The sum of the deaths is the total decrement, {math}`l_0-l_n`. The first value must be positive, later values non-negative and the table non-increasing.

## Parameters

`lx`
: One-dimensional series of lives, non-increasing, with a positive first value.

## Returns

A series of `lx.numel() − 1` non-negative values.

## Errors

Throws `dx_lx: lx[0] must be > 0`, `dx_lx: lx must be non-increasing` and `dx_lx: lx must be >= 0`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1: deaths per year

A cohort of 1,000 lives over four years.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  out.writeln(life::dx_lx(pluss::make_series({1000.0, 990.0, 978.0, 963.0, 945.0})).items<double>());
}
```

### Example 2: deaths add to the decrement

Their sum is the lives lost over the horizon.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const pluss::Series lx = pluss::make_series({1000.0, 990.0, 978.0, 963.0, 945.0});
  out.writeln("sum of deaths =", life::dx_lx(lx).sum().item<double>(), " l0 - ln =", 1000.0 - 945.0);
}
```

### Example 3: deaths as a share

Divide by the starting cohort to get the distribution of death by year.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  const pluss::Series qx = pluss::make_series({0.010, 0.012, 0.015, 0.019, 0.024});
  const pluss::Series lx = life::lx_qx(qx, 1.0);
  out.writeln(life::dx_lx(lx).items<double>());
  out.writeln(actuarial::mortality::from_qx(qx).lifetime_pmf().items<double>());
}
```

### Example 4: a single age

One value has no deaths.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  out.writeln(life::dx_lx(pluss::make_series({100.0})).numel());
}
```

### Example 5: the errors

A rising table, a negative life and a zero start.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

namespace actuarial = pluss::ma::actuarial;
namespace life = actuarial::life_contingencies;
namespace losses = actuarial::losses;
namespace models = actuarial::models;
namespace distr = pluss::subsp::stats::distr;
using namespace pluss::tils;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  const auto report = [&](const auto &call) {
    try {
      call();
    } catch (const std::exception &e) {
      std::string text(e.what());
      if (const auto cut = text.find("Triggered"); cut != std::string::npos) text.erase(cut);
      while (!text.empty() && text.back() == '\n') text.pop_back();
      out.writeln(text);
    }
  };
  report([&] { (void)life::dx_lx(pluss::make_series({10.0, 12.0})); });
  report([&] { (void)life::dx_lx(pluss::make_series({10.0, -1.0})); });
  report([&] { (void)life::dx_lx(pluss::make_series({0.0, 0.0})); });
}
```

